WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.340
Here's another type of quadrilateral.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.920
Let's name it ABCD.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:13.380
In this quadrilateral, both pairs of opposite sides are parallel.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.440
The first pair of opposite sides is AB and DC.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.680
We can see that AB is parallel to DC.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.180
We use two arrows in the same direction

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.100
to show that the sides are parallel.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.820
The second pair of opposite sides is AD and BC.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:36.980
We can also see that AD is parallel to BC.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.880
So we draw arrows like this.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.260
Such quadrilaterals are called parallelograms.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:48.020
Both pairs of opposite sides are parallel.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.940
This was the basic property of a parallelogram.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.960
In a parallelogram, the opposite sides are also equal.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.860
This side will be equal to this side.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.920
We can say that AB is equal to DC.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.780
This side will be equal to this side.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.840
AD is equal to BC

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.540
And guess what, in a parallelogram,

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.140
the opposite angles are also equal.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.500
Opposite angles are angles

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.080
which do not have a common side.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.280
This angle will be equal to this angle.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.180
Angle DAB is equal to angle DCB.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.260
And this angle will be equal to this angle.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.920
Angle ABC is equal to angle ADC.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:40.480
Remember, this is the basic property of a parallelogram.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.580
The opposite sides as well as the opposite angles are equal.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.440
Let's see a special case of a parallelogram.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:54.700
In this parallelogram, all the sides are equal to each other.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.580
This is a rhombus.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.880
So a rhombus is a parallelogram with all its sides equal.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.320
It will have all the properties of a parallelogram,

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.160
as well as this additional property that all its sites will be equal.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.660
There is another special case of a parallelogram.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.160
Let me draw it on a new page.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.440
Remember, the opposite sides have to be parallel.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:23.560
It is a quadrilateral drawn like this.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.460
The opposite sides of this quadrilateral are parallel.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.680
So it is a parallelogram.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.740
Let's name the quadrilateral ABCD.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.720
Why is it special?

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.000
All the angles in the quadrilaterals are right angles.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.840
This special case of parallelogram is called a rectangle.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.800
This is how a rectangle can be defined.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:53.100
It is a parallelogram with all angles being right angles.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.960
Just like in a parallelogram

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:58.580
the opposite sides of a rectangle are equal.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.260
This side will be equal to this side,

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.800
and this side will be equal to this one.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.720
Now it gets even more interesting.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.040
This quadrilateral is a special case of a rectangle.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:15.080
Let's call it PQRS.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:19.300
Like the rectangle, all its angles are right angles,

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.140
but it has an additional property.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.220
All Its sides are equal to each other.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.340
This type of quadrilateral is called a square.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.980
Basically, it is a rectangle with all its sides equal.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.760
The rectangle is the special case of the parallelogram.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.260
And this square is a special case of a rectangle.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.740
But wait, a square the opposite sides are parallel.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.340
So it is a parallelogram.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.220
All Its sides are also equal, so it's also a rhombus.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.480
Again, what is a rhombus ?

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.000
It is a quadrilateral with all its sides equal

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.560
and opposite sides parallel to each other.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:07.520
But how is the square different from a normal rhombus?

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.320
It is a rhombus in which all angles are right angles.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:16.040
Next, we will review all the types of quadrilaterals,

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:19.100
and how they are related to each other.

